      "content": "i've been tracking the orbital drift of the 'starlink-type' clusters over the last few nights and something is really off. the standard TLE data doesn't account for these micro-adjustments in the vector. i logged these specific timestamp/coordinate shifts from the 17th and they seem way too rhythmic to be just atmospheric drag or solar pressure. \n\n04:12:01 - 34.22N 118.45W (delta +0.004)\n04:12:45 - 34.25N 118.48W (delta -0.002)\n04:13:30 - 34.29N 118.51W (delta +0.009)\n04:14:15 - 34.33N 118.55W (delta -0.001)\n\nit's like they're pulsing. can you look at the intervals and the delta changes? is there any kind of non-mechanical pattern here or am i just seeing things?",
